  <!-- =========================================================================
       SECTION 7: DAILY NUTRITION CALCULATOR
       ========================================================================= -->
  <section id="section-calculator" class="app-section">
    <div class="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-12">
      <!-- Section Header -->
      <div class="max-w-3xl mb-8">
        <span class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-emerald-400 bg-emerald-500/10 px-3 py-1 rounded-full border border-emerald-500/30">
          Energy Thermodynamics
        </span>
        <h2 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-extrabold text-white mt-3">Daily Nutrition Calculator</h2>
        <p class="text-sm text-slate-300 mt-2">
          Calculate your estimated Basal Metabolic Rate (BMR), Total Daily Energy Expenditure (TDEE), and optimal macronutrient split using the Mifflin-St Jeor equation.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-12 gap-8">
        <!-- Input Form -->
        <div class="lg:col-span-5 fit-card p-6">
          <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-white mb-4 flex items-center gap-2">
            <span>⚙️</span> Your Physical Parameters
          </h3>

          <div class="space-y-4 text-xs">
            <!-- Age & Sex -->
            <div class="grid grid-cols-2 gap-3">
              <div>
                <label class="font-semibold text-slate-400 block mb-1">Age (Years)</label>
                <input type="number" id="calc-age" value="25" min="15" max="95" class="w-full p-2.5 bg-slate-900 border border-slate-700 rounded-lg text-white">
              </div>
              <div>
                <label class="font-semibold text-slate-400 block mb-1">Biological Sex</label>
                <select id="calc-sex" class="w-full p-2.5 bg-slate-900 border border-slate-700 rounded-lg text-white">
                  <option value="male">Male</option>
                  <option value="female">Female</option>
                </select>
              </div>
            </div>

            <!-- Height & Weight -->
            <div class="grid grid-cols-2 gap-3">
              <div>
                <label class="font-semibold text-slate-400 block mb-1">Height (cm)</label>
                <input type="number" id="calc-height" value="175" min="100" max="240" class="w-full p-2.5 bg-slate-900 border border-slate-700 rounded-lg text-white">
              </div>
              <div>
                <label class="font-semibold text-slate-400 block mb-1">Weight (kg)</label>
                <input type="number" id="calc-weight" value="70" min="30" max="250" class="w-full p-2.5 bg-slate-900 border border-slate-700 rounded-lg text-white">
              </div>
            </div>

            <!-- Activity Level -->
            <div>
              <label class="font-semibold text-slate-400 block mb-1">Daily Activity Level</label>
              <select id="calc-activity" class="w-full p-2.5 bg-slate-900 border border-slate-700 rounded-lg text-white">
                <option value="1.2">Sedentary (Desk job, little or no exercise)</option>
                <option value="1.375">Lightly Active (Light exercise 1-3 days/week)</option>
                <option value="1.55" selected>Moderately Active (Moderate exercise 3-5 days/week)</option>
                <option value="1.725">Very Active (Heavy training 6-7 days/week)</option>
                <option value="1.9">Extremely Active (Physical labor or double training days)</option>
              </select>
            </div>

            <!-- Fitness Goal -->
            <div>
              <label class="font-semibold text-slate-400 block mb-1">Fitness Target</label>
              <select id="calc-goal" class="w-full p-2.5 bg-slate-900 border border-slate-700 rounded-lg text-white">
                <option value="muscle-gain" selected>Lean Muscle Gain (+350 kcal surplus)</option>
                <option value="fat-loss">Fat Loss (-450 kcal deficit)</option>
                <option value="maintain">Maintenance (Weight equilibrium)</option>
                <option value="strength">Strength & Power (+200 kcal)</option>
                <option value="endurance">Endurance Stamina (+250 kcal)</option>
              </select>
            </div>

            <button id="calculate-nutrition-btn" class="w-full btn-primary justify-center py-3 text-xs rounded-lg mt-2">
              Calculate Nutritional Estimates ➔
            </button>
          </div>

          <div class="mt-4 p-3 bg-slate-900 rounded-lg border border-slate-800 text-[11px] text-slate-400 italic">
            *FitGuide equations provide evidence-based estimates. Actual metabolic rates vary with lean muscle mass, thermal environment, and endocrine health.
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Output Dashboard -->
        <div class="lg:col-span-7">
          <div id="calculator-results-container"></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- =========================================================================
       SECTION 8: PROTEIN / VITAMIN / IRON EXPLORER
       ========================================================================= -->
  <section id="section-explorer" class="app-section">
    <div class="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-12">
      <!-- Section Header -->
      <div class="max-w-3xl mb-8">
        <span class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-emerald-400 bg-emerald-500/10 px-3 py-1 rounded-full border border-emerald-500/30">
          Targeted Bioavailability
        </span>
        <h2 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-extrabold text-white mt-3">Protein, Iron & Vitamin Explorer</h2>
        <p class="text-sm text-slate-300 mt-2">
          Rank foods by nutrient density, understand the biology of heme vs non-heme iron absorption, and explore comprehensive vitamin profiles.
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- Explorer Navigation Tabs -->
      <div class="flex items-center gap-2 mb-8 border-b border-slate-800 pb-3">
        <button class="explorer-tab-btn px-5 py-2.5 rounded-xl text-xs font-bold bg-emerald-500 text-slate-950 transition-all cursor-pointer" data-explorer-tab="protein">
          🥩 Protein Density Ranking
        </button>
        <button class="explorer-tab-btn px-5 py-2.5 rounded-xl text-xs font-bold bg-slate-800 text-slate-300 hover:text-white transition-all cursor-pointer" data-explorer-tab="iron">
          🩸 Iron Absorption & Foods
        </button>
        <button class="explorer-tab-btn px-5 py-2.5 rounded-xl text-xs font-bold bg-slate-800 text-slate-300 hover:text-white transition-all cursor-pointer" data-explorer-tab="vitamins">
          💊 Vitamin Profiles & RDAs
        </button>
      </div>

      <!-- Tab View 1: Protein Explorer -->
      <div id="explorer-view-protein" class="explorer-view">
        <div class="fit-card p-6 mb-8 border-l-4 border-l-emerald-500">
          <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-white mb-2">Protein Bioavailability & Amino Acid Completeness</h3>
          <p class="text-xs text-slate-300 leading-relaxed">
            Animal proteins (dairy, eggs, poultry, fish) are "complete proteins", providing all 9 essential amino acids in optimal ratios. Plant proteins (dal, beans, grains) are outstanding and can achieve complete amino acid complementarity when paired together (e.g., Dal + Rice, Peanut Butter + Roti, Hummus + Bread).
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="space-y-3" id="protein-ranking-list"></div>
      </div>

      <!-- Tab View 2: Iron Explorer -->
      <div id="explorer-view-iron" class="explorer-view hidden">
        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-6 mb-8">
          <!-- Heme Iron -->
          <div class="fit-card p-6 border-l-4 border-l-red-500">
            <span class="text-xs font-bold text-red-400 uppercase tracking-wider block mb-1">Animal Tissue Form</span>
            <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-white mb-2">Heme Iron</h3>
            <p class="text-xs text-slate-300 leading-relaxed mb-3">
              Found in meat, poultry, and seafood. Bound within hemoglobin and myoglobin molecules. Highly bioavailable (~15-35% intestinal absorption) and minimally influenced by dietary inhibitors.
            </p>
            <div class="text-xs text-slate-400">Sources: Chicken, Fish, Liver, Eggs.</div>
          </div>

          <!-- Non-Heme Iron -->
          <div class="fit-card p-6 border-l-4 border-l-emerald-500">
            <span class="text-xs font-bold text-emerald-400 uppercase tracking-wider block mb-1">Plant & Fortified Form</span>
            <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-white mb-2">Non-Heme Iron</h3>
            <p class="text-xs text-slate-300 leading-relaxed mb-3">
              Found in lentils, spinach, ragi, and seeds. Has lower baseline absorption (~2-20%) because it exists in the ferric state (Fe3+).
            </p>
            <div class="text-xs text-slate-400">Sources: Palak, Ragi, Rajma, Sesame seeds, Dal.</div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Vitamin C Synergistic Effect Notice -->
        <div class="p-5 rounded-xl bg-gradient-to-r from-amber-950/40 to-slate-900 border border-amber-500/40 mb-8">
          <div class="flex items-start gap-3">
            <span class="text-2xl">🍋</span>
            <div class="text-xs text-slate-300 space-y-1">
              <strong class="text-amber-400 text-sm block">How Vitamin C Multiplies Iron Absorption:</strong>
              <p>Ascorbic acid (Vitamin C) acts as an electron donor, reducing insoluble ferric iron (Fe3+) into soluble ferrous iron (Fe2+) which readily binds to gut transport proteins. Squeezing fresh lemon juice onto Dal or eating an orange or Amla with spinach can boost iron uptake by up to <strong>300%</strong>.</p>
              <p class="text-slate-400 pt-1"><em>Caution: Avoid drinking tea or coffee within 60 minutes of iron-rich meals, as polyphenolic tannins bind iron and suppress absorption.</em></p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <h4 class="text-base font-bold text-white mb-4">Top Iron-Rich Foods in FitGuide:</h4>
        <div id="iron-foods-list" class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3 gap-4"></div>
      </div>

      <!-- Tab View 3: Vitamin Profiles Explorer -->
      <div id="explorer-view-vitamins" class="explorer-view hidden">
        <div class="mb-6">
          <span class="text-xs font-bold text-slate-400 uppercase tracking-wider block mb-2">Select a Vitamin to View Deep Profile:</span>
          <div id="vitamin-buttons-bar" class="flex flex-wrap gap-2"></div>
        </div>

        <div id="selected-vitamin-display"></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

